<h1>Patricia L. Tillman</h1>
<p>Governor &amp; Lieutenant Governor, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Declared write-in.</p>
<p>These names are not printed on the ballot. To vote for one, write the name in the blank write-in space for that office and fill in the oval (on a touchscreen, follow the write-in steps on screen). Votes count only for write-ins who filed a declaration. The Chicago Board of Elections does not post those names, so this list comes from the Cook County Clerk&#39;s list and campaign announcements; election judges at your polling place have the official one.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Declared write-in candidate; the name is not printed on the ballot. Running with Joseph L. Mosley. No platform or campaign website found. The State Board of Elections removed the ticket from the March Democratic primary ballot in December 2025 for having too few valid petition signatures.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Ran as a write-in candidate for alderperson of the 21st Ward in 2023.</p>
